EXECUTION MODE

Complete this process iteratively:

1. Inspect the entire Figma file.
2. Inventory all screens, workflows, components, variants, and states.
3. Identify reusable components and Atomic Design classifications.
4. Identify backend services, APIs, validation rules, permissions, and data contracts.
5. Identify missing or ambiguous requirements.
6. Design the Next.js frontend architecture.
7. Propose epics, stories, tasks, and subtasks.
8. Review the backlog for missing work, duplication, incorrect dependencies, and oversized stories.
9. Refine the backlog until all Figma screens and workflows are covered.
10. Search Jira for existing tickets to avoid duplication.
11. Create the Jira epics first.
12. Create the stories and tasks under their correct epics.
13. Create subtasks under the correct parent stories.
14. Attach the appropriate Figma screenshots.
15. Establish Jira dependency relationships.
16. Verify every created Jira ticket.
17. Produce a detailed final Jira creation report.

The request authorizes Jira issue creation. Do not stop after merely proposing the backlog unless Jira or Figma permissions prevent creation.

If a business-critical ambiguity would cause incorrect implementation, document a reasonable assumption and create a clarification ticket. Continue creating all tickets that are not blocked by that ambiguity.

