STORY-SIZING RULES

Every story must:

* Deliver one clear and demonstrable outcome
* Have one primary responsibility
* Be independently testable
* Avoid unrelated frontend and backend changes
* Be approximately one to three development days where practical
* Contain objective acceptance criteria
* Identify dependencies and blockers
* Be split when it covers multiple independent workflows
* Be split when it has more than approximately eight substantial acceptance criteria
* Be split when several developers could implement its parts independently

Use subtasks for implementation steps within one deliverable.

Use separate stories when work can be independently:

* Prioritized
* Assigned
* Implemented
* Tested
* Released
* Blocked

